[0m\nThinking: Let me explore the codebase to understand the structure and find the knowledge base management page with the left sidebar issue.\n[0m• [0mExplore knowledge base sidebar[90m Explore Agent[0m\n[0m✓ [0mExplore knowledge base sidebar[90m Explore Agent[0m\nThinking: The agent found the issue. The sidebar on the knowledge page starts hidden because there\'s no `active` class on the `<aside class=\"sidebar\" id=\"sidebar\">` element, and unlike the main chat page, there\'s no `initSidebar()` call to add the `.active` class on desktop.\n\nLet me look at the specific files to confirm and plan the fix.\n[0m→ [0mRead templates/knowledge.html[90m [offset=930, limit=50][0m\n[0m→ [0mRead static/js/main.js[90m [offset=85, limit=20][0m\nThinking: Now let me check if `knowledge.html` calls `initSidebar()` anywhere and what JS is included at the bottom of the page.\n[0m✱ [0mGrep \"initSidebar|DOMContentLoaded\"[90m in templates/knowledge.html · 1 match[0m\n[0m→ [0mRead templates/knowledge.html[90m [offset=2140, limit=20][0m\nThinking: The `knowledge.html` page has a `DOMContentLoaded` listener but it doesn\'t call `initSidebar()`. Let me see what it does.\n[0m→ [0mRead templates/knowledge.html[90m [offset=1235, limit=40][0m\nThinking: Now I can see the issue clearly. The `knowledge.html` page has a `DOMContentLoaded` listener that calls:\n- `applyThemeFromCache()`\n- `loadUserInfo()`\n- `loadKnowledgeBases()`\n- `initEventListeners()`\n\nBut it **never calls `initSidebar()`**, which is the function in `main.js` that adds the `.active` class to the sidebar on desktop (window width > 768px).\n\nWithout the `.active` class, the sidebar is hidden because `.sidebar { transform: translateX(-100%); }` in the CSS.\n\nThe fix is simple: add `initSidebar()` call in the DOMContentLoaded handler. But I also need to make sure `initSidebar()` is available — let me check if `main.js` is included in `knowledge.html`.\n[0m✱ [0mGrep \"main\\.js\"[90m in te