 document.body.setAttribute(\'data-theme\', prefersDark ? \'dark\' : \'light\');\n    }\n})();\n```\n\nThis actually **DOES** support system theme - when there\'s no cached theme, it uses `prefers-color-scheme: dark` to determine the theme. But the issue is: when user visits another page and sets a custom theme, that gets stored in localStorage and then gets applied to research page too.\n\n2. **What other pages do**: Other pages like index.html, knowledge.html, tools.html only do:\n```javascript\nvar cachedTheme = localStorage.getItem(\'user_theme\');\nif (cachedTheme) {\n    document.body.setAttribute(\'data-theme\', cachedTheme);\n}\n```\n\nThey don\'t have the fallback to system theme at all - they just use localStorage and nothing else. If there\'s no cached theme, they just don\'t set any data-theme attribute.\n\nWait, but that doesn\'t make sense either - they need to have some theme. Let me check again...\n\nActually looking at index.html lines 7-14, it only sets data-theme if cachedTheme exists. But style.css has default dark theme variables (lines 8-24), so the default would be dark. But that\'s not \"following system theme\" either.\n\nThe user says \"其他页面\" (other pages) - they want to follow system theme. Let me re-read the user\'s request:\n\"最新研究这个页面主题色和其他页面不一致，需要修复为随系统主题色\"\n\n\nSo the problem is that research.html has different behavior than other pages. It\'s not that other pages follow system theme - it\'s that research page is different. But looking at the code, both research.html and index.html use localStorage, and neither truly follows system theme. The research.html actually tries to follow system theme when there\'s no cached theme, while index.html doesn\'t even try. Wait, maybe I\'m misunderstanding. Let me check if other pages are truly following system theme or if they\'re all just using localStorage or default dark.\n\nLooking at research.html, it checks localStorage first, then falls back to system preference. But index.html and tools.html only check localStorage - they don\'t have the system preference fallback at all. This means when there\'s no cached theme, index.html gets the default dark from style.css, while research.html gets the system preference. That\'s the inconsistency.\n\nThe solution is to remove the system preference fallback from research.html so it matches how other pages work - only use what\'s stored in localStorage. This way both pages will behave identically when there\'s no cached theme.\n[0m→ [0mRead templates/research.html[90m [limit=20][0m\nThinking: 现在我理解问题了。\n\n**其他页面**（如 index.html、knowledge.html 等）的主题色处理：\n- 只从 `localStorage.getItem(\'user_theme\')` 读取缓存的主题\n- 如果没有缓存，则保持默认样式（由 style.css 中的 `:root` 定义 - 深色主题）\n\n**最新研究页面**（research.html）的问题：\n- 额外添加了 `prefers-color-scheme: dark` 检测，会自动设置 `data-theme` 属性\n- 这导致如果用户没有设置过主题，系统会强制设为 dark，可能与其他页面不一致\n\n**解决方案**：\n将 research.html 的主题检测逻辑改为与其他页面一致 - 只读取 localStorage，不自动检测系统主题：\n\n```javascript\n(function() {\n    var cachedTheme = localStorage.getItem(\'user_theme\');\n    if (cachedTheme) {\n        document.body.setAttribute(\'data-theme\', cachedTheme);\n    }\n})();\n```\n\n这就是问题所在 - research.html 有额外的 `prefers-color-scheme` 检测逻辑，而其他页面没有。修复方法就是移除这个自动检测逻辑。\n[0m\n[0m← [0mEdit templates/research.html\nIndex: /home/yangkai/github/arc-logi/chat/templates/research.html\n===================================================================\n--- /home/yangkai/github/arc-logi/chat/templates/research.html\n+++ /home/yangkai/github/arc-logi/chat/templates/research.html\n@@ -8,11 +8,8 @@\n     (function() {\n         var cachedTheme = localStorage.getItem(\'user_theme\');\n         if (cachedTheme) {\n             document.body.setAttribute(\'data-theme\', cachedTheme);\n-        } else {\n-            var prefersDark = window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia(\'(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\').matches;\n-            document.body.setAttribute(\'data-theme\', prefersDark ? \'dark\' : \'light\');\n         }\n     })();\n </script>